\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. From  every stormy wind that blows,
\par From every swelling  tide of woes,
\par There is a calm, a sure retreat;
\par This found beneath the mercy-seat.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. There is a place where Jesus sheds
\par The oil of gladness on our heads-
\par A place than all beside more sweet;
\par It is the blood-stained mercy-seat
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. There is a spot where spirits blend,
\par And  friend holds fellowship with friend;
\par Though sundered far, by faith they meet
\par Around one common mercy-seat.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. There, there on eagle wing we soar,
\par And time and sense seem all no more;
\par And heaven comes down our souls to greet,
\par And glory crowns the mercy-seat.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

